// PARAM: --analysis int
// precision/01-refinement_beats_components.vimp with the nondet seed removed,
// which is the whole difference between it proving y == 2 and this not.
//
// An unwritten int32 local is unconstrained: VIMP's initial stores pin the
// globals to zero and say nothing about locals, and teval reads a variable
// without normalizing. So a store holding 2 + 2^32 satisfies y + 1 == 3 while
// y == 2 is false, and UNKNOWN is not merely imprecise here -- PROVED would be
// wrong for that store.
//
// The components show exactly where it stops: backward-filtering the guard
// yields congruence == 2 (mod 4294967296) and parity Even, both exact, while
// the interval stays [-inf,+inf] because nothing has said y is an int32.
// There is no bounded interval for the reduction to meet the congruence
// against, so the product cannot collapse it to the single value 2.
//
// This is the initialization half of the styped gap, and it is what slice A6b
// of docs/VAR_ID_MIGRATION.md closes: a declaration-derived seed bounds the
// cell at its kind's range, the congruence meets it at 2, and this fixture
// should then move to precision/.
void main() {
  int32 x, y;
  if (y + 1 == 3) {
    x := 1;
    __voblint_check(y == 2) // UNKNOWN
  } else {
    x := 0
  }
}
